    "created_at": "2022-03-23T14:59:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-23T14:59:08Z",
    "body": "I would support, and be willing to do spec work for, deprecating object and embed. They are very bad. The less people use them, the more we can work on security improvements such as #7327 and the auto-sizing issue mentioned here, as well as simplifications such as generally unifying them with iframe logic as much as possible.\r\n\r\nI think the main question is whether we want to have a carveout to still allow same-origin interactive-SVG `<object>`, because it has autosizing behavior which is hard to replicate, and if constrained to same-origin, is not a security issue. (The HTML spec itself uses it for that purpose.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1076469252/reactions",
